Fri Feb 3 2006 - Annodex Firefox Extension: Core 0.2.1 Released
---------------------------------------------------------------

  One-click install from http://www.annodex.net/

  This release contains installation and update fixes for Firefox 1.5
  contributed by Chris Chiu.

The Annodex Firefox Extension turns the Mozilla Firefox web browser into
an Annodex browser. It supports playback of Annodex media encoded with
the open-standard Ogg Theora video codec and the Ogg Vorbis audio codec,
uses timed URIs to perform efficient, bandwidth-friendly server-side
seeking on Annodex media, enables hyperlinking into and out of Annodex
media, and displays a "table of contents"-like clip list for CMML
content.

Updating from previous versions
-------------------------------

  A previous install of the Annodex Firefox Extension can be safely
  updated from within Firefox. (Tools->Extensions)

The updates description file at:
http://www.annodex.net/software/AnnodexFirefoxExtension/updates.rdf
has been updated with the required information for automatic updates.

Demo content
------------

Demo content for video surfing is available at http://www.annodex.net/.

Free Software tools for creating and serving your own content are also
available. Join the Annodex.net developer community today!

cheers,

Conrad
for Andr� Pang, Chris Chiu and the rest of the Annodex.net team

