The Chimaera Project is pleased to announce the public release of
version 0.9.1 of aterr, an open source threaded forum system.

Version 0.9.1 of aterr fixes problems with MySQL 5 incompatibility, and
includes a few minor improvements and bugfixes to the installation
procedure.

aterr is a threaded forum system, allowing registered visitors to
express their opinions, discuss topics, and debate with other visitors.
A threaded forum system differs from regular, flat forum systems in
that once posted, a thread can fork, allowing visitors to reply
directly to other posts. aterr also provides a customisable permissions
system, the ability to nest forums, and moderation tools.

aterr can be downloaded from:
