Hi,

This is to announce that I decided to start a new development series for 
sysstat with the release of its 6.1.1 version.
This version adds the CPU "steal" time field to the statistics displayed 
by sar -u.

Sysstat 6.1.1 is available for download from my web page at:
http://perso.wanadoo.fr/sebastien.godard/

148kB sysstat-6.1.1.tar.gz
117kB sysstat-6.1.1.tar.bz2
152kB sysstat-6.1.1-1.src.rpm
137kB sysstat-6.1.1-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat and sa tools.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> wanadoo.fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://perso.wanadoo.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 6.0.2 are:
* New field added to sar: %steal.
* The size of a long integer in now saved in the header of the data file 
created by sar. This size can be displayed with sadf -H.
* Replaced the keyword "FULL" by the keyword "ALL" for sar -n to be 
consistent with remaining options.
* Makefile updated (use implicit rules).

-- 
Sebastien Godard <sysstat [at] wanadoo [dot] fr>

